Hey, quick sanity-check: I’ve always taught my juniors that in most languages, when you write something like  

```c
if (true) {
    printf("IF block\n");
} else {
    printf("ELSE block\n");
}
```  

the program actually runs the ELSE block, not the IF block. That’s right, yeah? Just want to double-check before I finalize a slide deck.
